From fcb88211d861634b121e089a1bfc18380cf1b306 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlund <mlund@localhost>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:43:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] [MOS] Add nonallocatable 32-bit imaginary registers

Model each RL as two RS subregisters and support physical copies and
symbol lowering. Group RL aliases during zero-page CSR allocation.

Keep Imag32 nonallocatable because linker scripts may place adjacent RS
registers apart.

[Rebased onto llvm-mos 06bc967d2668 for the #320 series: from llvm-mos/llvm-mos#594 head 7b80f7e18768. MOSImagReg32 takes a bits<32> number, matching the 32-bit MOSReg numbering introduced by #571; every other changed line is as posted.]
